        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Anthony D. \"Tony\" Saletan\n- Songs: \"Kum ba yah\"\n- Roles: folk singer, educator\n- Topics: folk music, song rediscovery, folk revival\n\nFacts:\n- \"Kum ba yah\" was first recorded in August 1926.\n- \"Kum ba yah\" later became a standard campfire song in Scouting and summer camps.\n- \"Kum ba yah\" enjoyed broader popularity during the folk revival of the 1950s and 1960s.\n- Anthony D. \"Tony\" Saletan is an American folk singer and educator.\n- Anthony D. \"Tony\" Saletan was responsible for the modern rediscovery of \"Kum ba yah\" and another of the genre's best-known songs.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
