        "original_id": "bcae7025-acfa-579c-8d5e-f362bef5116a",
        "text": "Anthony D. \"Tony\" Saletan is an American folk singer and educator, who is responsible for the modern rediscovery of two of the genre's best-known songs, one being Kum ba yah, first recorded in August 1926. It became a standard campfire song in Scouting and summer camps and enjoyed broader popularity during the folk revival of the 1950s and 1960s.",
